Let $P\left(x_{1}, y_{1}\right)$ be the mid-point of a chord of $x^{2}+y^{2}=r^{2}$.
Its equation is
$\begin{aligned}
S_{1} &=S_{11} \Rightarrow x_{1} x+y_{1} y=x_{1}^{2}+y_{1}^{2} \\
\text{ or } y &=\left(-\frac{x_{1}}{y_{1}}\right) x+\frac{x_{1}^{2}+y_{1}^{2}}{y_{1}}
\end{aligned}$
The line $y=m x+c$ is a tangent to the hyperbola only if
$\begin{aligned}
c^{2} &=a^{2} m^{2}-b^{2} \\
\therefore \quad \frac{\left(x_{1}^{2}+y_{1}^{2}\right)^{2}}{y_{1}^{2}} &=\frac{a^{2} x_{1}^{2}}{y_{1}^{2}}-b^{2}
\end{aligned}$
$\therefore$ The locus of $P$ is
$\left(x^{2}+y^{2}\right)^{2}=a^{2} x^{2}-b^{2} y^{2}$
